Context: I am refactoring my Chat App to match a high-end, premium minimalist aesthetic inspired by Jordan Hughes and Emil Kowalski. I am using shadcn/ui, Tailwind CSS, and Framer Motion.

Task: Refactor the [Target File/Component] with the following UI/UX constraints:

Typography & Spacing:

Use Geist Sans for primary text and Geist Mono for secondary data/timestamps.

Increase whitespace significantly. Use generous padding (e.g., p-6 or p-8) and consistent gaps (gap-4 or gap-6).

Visual Style (The Hughes Look):

Borders: Replace heavy borders with subtle, low-opacity ones (e.g., border-zinc-200/50 or dark:border-zinc-800/50).

Surfaces: Use a pure white (#FFFFFF) or very deep black (#09090b) background. Use a subtle offset for sidebars (e.g., bg-zinc-50/50).

Shadows: Use very soft, diffused shadows (shadow-sm) or no shadows at all, relying on borders for separation.

Radius: Ensure all shadcn components use a consistent rounded-xl (12px) or rounded-2xl.

Micro-interactions (The Kowalski Touch):

Integrate Framer Motion for all transitions.

Use "Spring" physics instead of linear eases (e.g., type: "spring", stiffness: 400, damping: 30).

Implement layoutId for active states (like selecting a chat) so the background highlight "slides" smoothly.

Add subtle hover scales (whileHover={{ scale: 1.01 }}) and press effects (whileTap={{ scale: 0.98 }}).

Refined UI Elements:

Make the search bars and inputs very clean: minimal borders, subtle focus rings.

Ensure message bubbles have refined tail-less designs with high-contrast text.

Goal: The interface should feel "airy," precise, and sophisticated. Avoid any "default" or "generic" AI-generated look.